From c112619db9fa087519c3b78ffe17df007d397f15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luca Bruni <luca.bruni@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:21:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] gfx9-win: EXPERIMENTAL dxg-gfx9-trap-handler

Opt-in prototype (DXG_TRAP=1), not for upstream as is.

On gfx9 under Windows ROCr, device traps (assert, abort, __builtin_trap) have
no handler that reports them: the PM4-emulated queues have no consumer for
the s_sendmsg interrupt the regular handlers rely on. With DXG_TRAP=1 ROCr
binds a small gfx9 handler that records the trap (ttmp0-15, STATUS, TRAPSTS,
HW_ID) in a mailbox at TMA and ends the wave. If the KMD accepts the
set-trap-handler escape, the thunk sets TRAP_PRESENT per dispatch and fails
the queue with HSA_STATUS_ERROR_EXCEPTION after the dispatch's fence.
DXG_TRAP_DIAG prints the escape result and the trap record.

Built at the 7.15 nightly pin. On gfx90c the legacy KMD (2319) refuses the
escape, so the handler stays unbound; kept for KMDs that accept it. Handler
source: docs/gfx9-windows/trap-prototype/dxg_trap_gfx9.s in TheRock.

Rebased onto the current pin: the KMD debugger version check keeps upstream's
1.2 to 2.x range, and the trap check follows upstream's sync_point fence wait.
Not rebuilt or retested after the rebase.
